 "limits": [
  "the key has to be a literal string; a key held in a variable is the same blind spot E619 has, so a line whose key is computed is published as its literal only",
  "a read counts when it indexes the same literal key, whatever the object: m[\"k\"] on a different dict in the same function would satisfy the duplicate test -- the population is small enough (34 lines) that each row carries the key and its other read lines for a reader to check",
  "reads inside a nested function definition are not counted for the outer function, while E619's dead-local test does count a load in a nested scope; the two rules differ on purpose and the conflict is one-directional (E619's is more permissive about what makes a local live)",
  "reachability is E622's measurement inside one module; a holder called only by an importer is outside both studies",
  "this script excludes itself and its smoke leg, and keeps E622's self-exclusion set, so the population is the one E622 published"
